// A line break does not end `>>`, so an edit that starts a line inside one is
// an item of the output: it prints what it would build and the variable does
// not change. `check` says so, in the three engines (GLB-137, decided by the
// author 2026-10-16). Spreading one output over several lines is a form
// programs use, and an assignment there still starts a statement.
d = #(x: 1)
v = [3, 1]
>> "a"
d["z"]$~ 2
>> ¶
>> "b"
v$+ 5
>> ¶
>> "c"
v$^+
>> ¶
>> "varias "
   "lineas" ¶
n = 1
>> "d"
n = 7
>> n ¶
>> d v ¶
